there's currently lots of confusion and  debate over who is a socialist and this  has become super prominent in right-wing  political discourse as of late you might  remember that at the latest state of the  union address Donald Trump even loudly  proclaimed that the United States is  never going to be a socialist country  and I want to dig into this today first  of all as I've said before Trump can't  actually control whether the US ever  becomes a socialist country and you  can't control what happens after his  presidency but the most important  reaction to have when Trump loudly  proclaims that is that there's no big  clamoring for actual socialism from  anyone in power in the United States the  furthest left ideas that are prominent  in the u.s. from elected officials are  socially democratic ideas with the  tiniest sprinkling of people in Congress  who actually are open to the idea of  socializing the means of production but  basically the furthest left ideas that  are part of the dialogue are social  democratic ideas number two - very very  crudely summarize it socialism sort of  split off in the late 19th century one  direction was the Stalinist Leninist  line which became communistic and then  there's the social democracy line which  became most prominently early or late in  the 19th century the Swedish Social  Democratic Party but that doesn't  actually matter because this is a known  tactic the tactic is smear as communist  anything that is socially Democratic  that that's the the tactic that we've  seen for a very long time Edward  Herrmann and Noam Chomsky write about  this in their 1988 book manufacturing  consent we have to be able to really  think about this we have to separate our  personal beliefs from factual history as  people know I'm not a communist but I'm  acknowledging that communism has been  smeared as a propaganda method dating  all the way back to the early 20th  century in the United States and the  reason that this can happen the reason  that social democracy can  smeared under the umbrella of communism  is because a lot of people don't really  understand what social democracy is  versus socialism versus communism so  it's a tactic that works really really  well I don't want to give a full history  lesson here and we've gone into the  differences between socialism and  communism and social democracy but what  you have to understand is that most of  the American left is not socialist and  it's also not communist to the extent  that they even know the differences  between those ideologies and social  democracy because the right accuses  people like me Social Democrats of being  communists or socialists we immediately  end up on the defensive we on the left  end up having to defend what is  socialism or communism we end up miss  handling it we end up sounding sometimes  like the anti-communist reactionaries  that have been in the United States  since the early 20th century when no  one's actually talking about communism  so it's a really good tactic that the  right uses it's a brilliant smear you  say hey you know what um we could learn  a lot from the health care system of the  UK or from Canada or Sweden or  Switzerland and in comes the right and  they say that is a communist idea that's  a socialist idea the next part of the  conversation when someone says let's see  how we can improve our healthcare system  the next part of the conversation should  be you know what we should we should  discuss is Medicare for all the best  path forward or would we be better off  with a nationalized care delivery system  and a nonprofit health insurance  apparatus or would the german system be  better than the swiss system or what  elements of the canadian system would be  good that's the the way the conversation  should go you often can't even get there  because in comes the right saying that  socialist that's communist it's a  government takeover it's anti-american  and what the left ends up having to do  or ends up doing anyway is arguing about  whether health care for all is socialist  it's the wrong debate it  worked for 100 years it fragments the  left particularly because it makes the  small portion of the left that is  actually socialistic come out and say we  are socialists and that's a good thing  that's not the majority of the left the  demonization of communism might not  really seem important to Social  Democrats because we're not communists  but it's very damn or damaging because  it creates this sort of false dichotomy  between Communists and anti-communists  the reality is there's no threat of  communism in the United States Social  Democrats who believe in a mixed economy  and healthcare for all don't think about  communism very much what we're talking  about is modernizing our basic systems  the way that many rich countries have  done but when they draw the line as  either you're a communist or you're an  anti-communist  it makes the Left split and it makes the  left start to sound like reactionaries  and we end up losing so there's two  sides to this number one we should  accept that either way they are going to  smear Social Democratic ideas as  communist ideas these are capitalist  ideas they exist in capitalist systems  whether it's universal health care  tuition free college living wages they  will say these are communist ideas they  are not we should expect that and we  should know how to deal with it but the  one word of caution to the left is we  also shouldn't help them out by saying  we are democratic socialists when we are  Social Democrats there's a number of  elected officials in the Democratic  Party that have made this mistake they  call themselves Democratic socialists  when they are not that makes it easier  for the right to fracture the left for  the right to smear the left as  socialists  let's not make it easier for them let's  call ourselves Social Democrats if that  look that's what we are if you're a  socialist by all means call yourself a  socialist there is no advantage to using  the term Democratic Socialist if it  doesn't actually apply it just makes the  right smear tactics more effective but  understand this has been going on for a  very very long time and  should not fall for it
 

